      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] ❌ **Changes Requested** — Please split this CL and add automated tests. [[trajectory](http://go/tj/cns/gg-d/home/tomhughes@google.com/review_trajectories/cl6904834_d80317be-be64-4c15-b291-98cd052e8179.pb)]\n\n### Review Summary\n**Functionality**: The core flash operations and protection flag mappings are logically sound.\n**Architecture \u0026 Component Fit**: The driver matches the existing `cros_flash` abstraction correctly and places logic in the expected layers.\n**Code Simplicity**: I left a few inline comments on `zephyr/drivers/cros_flash/cros_flash_rtkfp.c` to flatten conditionals, remove redundant error checking paths in `cros_flash_rtkfp_protect_at_boot`, and delete unused variables.\n**Idiomaticity \u0026 Readability**: Good use of Zephyr\u0027s API and idiomatic C macros.\n**Security**: Software write protection correctly enforces monotonic extending-only changes when the hardware WP pin is asserted.\n**Testing**: Missing automated test coverage. Even for hardware drivers, pure logic such as `cros_flash_rtkfp_get_protect_flags` and `flash_check_prot_reg`—or the driver as a whole using Zephyr\u0027s `emul` framework for SPI flashes—can and must be unit tested. Please add Zephyr tests under `zephyr/test/` to cover these behaviors.\n**CL Size \u0026 Scope**: `Size: L (+516, -7)`. This CL is too large and bundles the definitions with the entire driver implementation. It must be split into smaller, atomic CLs. Suggested split plan:\n- CL 1: Add the foundational definitions (`common/spi_flash_reg.c`) and configuration files (`Kconfig`, `prj.conf`, `flash_chip.h`).\n- CL 2: Introduce the `cros_flash_rtkfp` driver implementation along with its unit tests.\n**Commit Message**: The commit message is correctly formatted, but `TEST\u003dNone` should be updated with the actual `zmake test` or `twister` command once unit tests are added.\n\nTAG\u003dagy\nCONV\u003d2c043ed0-dea2-4715-a254-32a7c315004e",
