      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review]\nThe error handling logic here duplicates the restoration of `cros_flash_rtkfp_sw_protect` in both the success and failure branches. Furthermore, the `if (!ret)` check at line 476 is always true, because if `ret` were non-zero earlier, the function would have already returned at line 451 or 471.\n\nThis entire block can be simplified significantly by unconditionally restoring the software protect if it was enabled, avoiding the duplicated error paths:\n\n```c\n\tret \u003d flash_write_prot_reg(dev, FLASH_PROTECTION_START, new_prot_end);\n\n\t/* Always re-enable SW protect if it was enabled before. */\n\tif (was_sw_protected) {\n\t\tint ret2 \u003d cros_flash_rtkfp_sw_protect(dev, true);\n\t\tif (ret2) {\n\t\t\tLOG_ERR(\"Failed to restore SW protect\");\n\t\t\t/* Panic due to security related issue. Flash protection\n\t\t\t * state is unknown. */\n\t\t\tk_panic();\n\t\t}\n\t\tdata-\u003esw_protected \u003d 1;\n\t}\n\n\tif (!ret) {\n\t\tLOG_DBG(\"set AT_BOOT\");\n\t}\n\treturn ret;\n```\n[🔗](http://go/tj/cns/gg-d/home/tomhughes@google.com/review_trajectories/cl6904834_d80317be-be64-4c15-b291-98cd052e8179.pb)",
